package webkit

// Prompt teaches agents to give a tool an interactive web frontend with the
// kit. It is short (tool descriptions are cut); kit/README.md, in the
// sandbox at /opt/tradera/webkit/README.md, has the whole guide.
const Prompt = `Interactive frontends: when people want to interact with a tool (operate it, forms, orders, filters, a dashboard they use, a console), build an interactive web page for it instead of relying on a generated frontend or ui_compose (those show results; a page does things). Write it in the sandbox (plain HTML is best), serve it, and expose it with proxy_create {port, start, title, tool}: it opens on the desk as the tool's card window, on the web, phones and desktops.
The page uses Tradera's web UI kit, so it looks exactly like the app and follows its theme: in <head> <link rel="stylesheet" href="/_tradera/kit/tradera-ui.css"><script src="/_tradera/kit/tradera-ui.js"></script>, <body class="t-page">. Every app component is a <t-…> element with the same props (kebab-case attributes, JSON values): t-column/t-row/t-grid (min-column-width)/t-card/t-section/t-tabs, t-text (variant h1-h5|body|caption), t-stat, t-chart (type line|area|bar|candlestick|pie|…; data, x, series|y), t-table (data, columns [{field, type, format}], search, selection), t-key-value, t-badge, t-quote, t-order-book, t-button (variant primary|tonal|…), t-text-field, t-dropdown, t-segmented-control, t-slider, t-switch, t-form, t-modal, t-callout, t-empty-state, t-skeleton…; gallery /_tradera/kit/gallery.html.
Calling the tool (the page's backend, as the person using it, through the Tradera API): declaratively call="Tool/microtool" args='{"city": {"path": "/form/city"}}' into="/fc" on buttons, forms (named fields become args) and <t-data call args into every> (loads, and reloads when bound args change; /fc__loading, /fc__error); in script await Tradera.call('Tool', 'microtool', args) (its value), Tradera.tools(), Tradera.show(tool, {microtool, args}). Data: Tradera.data (get/set paths); bind with bind-value="/form/city" or {"path": "/x"}; inputs write back; <t-show when>, <t-list each="/rows"><template>…</template></t-list>; client actions {"functionCall": {"call": "setValue|toggle|increment|showToast", …}}; formats number:2, compact, percent, currency:USD, date. Never hard-code colors or a theme (var(--t-primary), --t-series-1…).
Full guide: cat /opt/tradera/webkit/README.md (copy /opt/tradera/webkit/* to _tradera/kit/ in the served folder to check the page locally).`
